thag16.8:13.1 starts: Some tame with a blunt stick,
thag16.8:13.2 starts: with hooks, & with whips
thag16.8:13.3 starts: But without blunt or bladed weapons
thag16.8:13.4 starts: I was tamed by the one who is
thag17.2:24.1 starts: On either side is death,
thag17.2:24.2 starts: it’s not non-death, ahead or behind.
thag17.2:24.3 starts: Practice, don’t perish.
thag17.2:24.4 starts: Don’t let the moment pass you by.
thag17.2:29.1 starts: You shouldn’t trust in this way
thag17.2:29.2 starts: some householders or those gone forth.
thag17.2:29.3 starts: Having been good, they become bad.
thag17.2:29.4 starts: Having been bad, they become good.
thag17.2:31.1 starts: The concentration of one
thag17.2:31.2 starts: dwelling in heedfulness
thag17.2:31.3 starts: doesn’t waver,
thag17.2:31.4 starts: whether he is honored or not.
thag16.8:18.1 starts: They’re addicted to heedlessness
thag16.8:18.2 starts: —dullards, fools—
thag16.8:18.3 starts: while one who is wise
thag16.8:18.4 starts: as his highest wealth.
thag16.8:22.1 starts: Where once I stayed here & there
thag16.8:22.2 starts: in the wilderness,
thag16.8:22.3 starts: in mountains,
thag16.8:22.4 starts: caves—
thag16.8:26.1 starts: The Teacher has been served by me;
thag16.8:26.2 starts: the Awakened One’s bidding,
thag16.8:26.3 starts: the guide to becoming, uprooted;
thag16.8:26.4 starts: the heavy load, laid down.
thag17.2:2.1 starts: Eating moist or dry food,
thag17.2:2.2 starts: he shouldn’t be heavily sated.
thag17.2:2.3 starts: With unfilled belly, with measured food,
thag17.2:2.4 starts: the monk should wander
thag17.2:3.1 starts: Leaving four or five mouthfuls uneaten,
thag17.2:3.2 starts: he should drink water:
thag17.2:3.3 starts: This is enough
thag17.2:3.4 starts: for the easeful abiding
thag17.2:4.1 starts: And he covers himself with a proper robe
thag17.2:4.2 starts: enough for that purpose:
thag17.2:4.3 starts: This is enough
thag17.2:4.4 starts: for the easeful abiding
thag17.2:5.1 starts: As he sits cross-legged,
thag17.2:5.2 starts: it doesn’t rain on his knees:
thag17.2:5.3 starts: This is enough
thag17.2:5.4 starts: for the easeful abiding
thag17.2:11.1 starts: In village or wilds,
thag17.2:11.2 starts: valley, plateau:
thag17.2:11.3 starts: that place is delightful
thag17.2:11.4 starts: where arahants dwell.
thag17.2:13.1 starts: Regard him as one who
thag17.2:13.2 starts: points out
thag17.2:13.3 starts: the wise one who
thag17.2:13.4 starts: Stay with this sort of sage.
thag17.2:13.5 starts: For the one who stays
thag17.2:13.6 starts: things get better,
